WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.478
Lesson one.

00:00:01.478 --> 00:00:02.488
The task.

00:00:02.488 --> 00:00:08.252
Before we evolve anything, let's look closely at the problem our pilot has to solve.

00:00:08.852 --> 00:00:13.559
This is Lunar Lander, a small physics game from the Gymnasium library.

00:00:13.559 --> 00:00:22.187
The lander starts near the top of the screen with a random push, and it has to touch down softly on the pad between the two flags.

00:00:22.787 --> 00:00:26.353
Many times a second, the lander senses eight numbers.

00:00:26.353 --> 00:00:28.457
Its position, across and up.

00:00:28.457 --> 00:00:30.386
Its speed, across and up.

00:00:30.386 --> 00:00:33.075
Its tilt, and how fast it is spinning.

00:00:33.075 --> 00:00:37.350
And two switches that turn on when a leg touches the ground.

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:41.441
With those eight numbers, it picks one of four actions.

00:00:41.441 --> 00:00:42.494
Do nothing.

00:00:42.494 --> 00:00:44.101
Fire the left engine.

00:00:44.101 --> 00:00:46.318
Fire the main engine underneath.

00:00:46.318 --> 00:00:48.147
Or fire the right engine.

00:00:48.147 --> 00:00:53.767
The side engines push the lander sideways and spin it, and the main engine pushes it up.

00:00:54.367 --> 00:00:56.775
Every episode builds a new moon.

00:00:56.775 --> 00:01:03.575
The mountains are random, and the lander starts with a random shove, so no two flights are the same.

00:01:04.175 --> 00:01:06.696
The landing pad never moves, though.

00:01:06.696 --> 00:01:13.227
It's always in the middle, at the same height, and the lander's position inputs are measured from the pad.

00:01:13.227 --> 00:01:15.576
Zero, zero means right on target.

00:01:15.576 --> 00:01:24.642
During training, every pilot is tested on ten random moons, so evolution has to find a rule that works on all of them, instead of memorising one.

00:01:25.242 --> 00:01:27.733
The game keeps score while it flies.

00:01:27.733 --> 00:01:32.320
Moving toward the pad, slowing down, and staying level all earn a little.

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:36.357
Drifting away, speeding up, and tilting all cost a little.

00:01:36.957 --> 00:01:38.996
There are bigger events too.

00:01:38.996 --> 00:01:42.282
Each leg that touches the ground earns ten points.

00:01:42.282 --> 00:01:44.492
Coming to rest earns a hundred.

00:01:44.492 --> 00:01:46.661
Crashing costs a hundred.

00:01:47.261 --> 00:01:48.983
And fuel isn't free.

00:01:48.983 --> 00:01:53.105
Every frame the main engine fires costs a third of a point.

00:01:53.105 --> 00:01:56.234
The side engines cost a tenth as much.

00:01:56.834 --> 00:01:59.073
Add it all up over one flight.

00:01:59.073 --> 00:02:02.672
A score of two hundred or more counts as solved.
